# Didact Echo {4}{U} (3/2): "When this creature enters, draw a card" and "Descend 4 - This creature has flying as long as there are four or
# more permanent cards in your graveyard" (CR 207.2c, 110.4a, 604.1, 613.1f). Five Moxen pay it on turn 1 and it draws Thought Scour. On
# turn 3: Thought Scour on Bot1 mills two Plains (two permanent cards: no flying), Black Lotus is sacrificed for mana (three: no flying), a
# second Thought Scour on Bot2 puts two Ornithopters (plus the one Bot2 discarded to hand size on turn 2) into Bot2's graveyard (six
# permanent cards there, but only Bot1's count: no flying), and Mind Stone, sacrificed for its "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw
# a card", makes four: exactly the limit, flying. (The Scours, instants, are no permanent cards.)

